{
  "summary": "This experiment tested the scgpt RNA encoder in a multi-profile RNA-only setup with avgpool aggregation, comparing it to the scvi_n200 encoder. Validation accuracy (0.5305) and F1 (0.5152) were lower than the scvi_n200 baseline (config_004: 0.6501 accuracy, 0.6275 F1), suggesting scgpt may not outperform existing encoders in this configuration. The result indicates potential limitations of scgpt in multi-profile settings, though other factors like data characteristics or hyperparameters could influence the difference."
}

